course: dictionary
lesson: 8270
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one the writer means. The word right is a good example. «Show me the right answer» is about being correct. «Raise your right hand» is about a side of the body.
explain: Ask yourself what the sentence is about. In «His dad plays a fighting game with him, sitting right next to him», right means exactly, so the dad is very close. It does not mean correct or a side of the body.
explain: Test your meaning by putting it back in the sentence. If «sitting exactly next to him» still makes sense, you have the right meaning. Always read the whole sentence before you decide.
fact: Right means correct, with no mistake: «the right answer».
fact: Right can mean the side opposite to left: «my right hand».
fact: A right is something everyone should be allowed to have or do: «their languages, rights and lands».
fact: Right can mean exactly or at once, as in «right here» and «right now».
fact: Right can mean good, fair or proper: «It's not right to cheat.»
exercise: «Round 1: 8 of 20 right.» What does right mean here? | Turned over | The side opposite to left | *Correct, with no mistake | Shouting out loud
exercise: «Baptists baptise people by full immersion, which means going right under the water.» What does right mean here? | Correct | *Exactly, all the way | Fair | A side of the body
exercise: «Every child has a right to learn.» What is a right in this sentence? | Exactly at once | A square corner | *Something everyone should be allowed to have or do | The side opposite to left
test: «Put your right hand on the table.» What does right mean? | Exactly next to | Good and fair | Correct | *The side opposite to left
test: «It's not right to cheat.» What does right mean? | Correct, with no mistake | Exactly at once | *Good, fair or proper | A square corner
exam: Select the correct response: In «Every person has the right to learn», right means | *Entitlement, something a person should be allowed to have | Correct, with no mistake | The side opposite to left | Exactly at once
